ISA-L compression and decompression for BGZF blocks in HTSlib 1.24.

Port of the open HTSlib pull request https://github.com/samtools/htslib/pull/1908
(head a11ed5e3c3c2bad07e8691479ce6e3099ee741a0): bgzf.c and configure.ac,
without its CI workflow change. Changes to the pull request:

- _bgzf_compress_isal() returns -1 when the level buffer allocation fails.
- Without libdeflate, the zlib bgzf_compress() places the ISA-L branch after
  the stored-block branch; the pull request's placement does not compile.
- hts_feature_string() reports isal=yes or isal=no, so `samtools --version`
  shows whether ISA-L is used.

configure and config.h.in are regenerated with GNU Autoconf 2.73
(autoconf && autoheader), which reproduces the HTSlib 1.24 release files
byte for byte before this patch.

